Gap: `verify`'s visitor `|_| {}` to `layer_root`, and the `std` build's batched `chain_ends` - Aeneas gives an `FnMut` closure returning `()` a mistyped `call_mut`; the batched form runs through `keccak256::hash_many`, per-host SIMD that is opaque in the extraction
Two changes.

`verify` calls `layer_root_unwatched`, added here: `layer_root` without the visitor, over
`keccak256::path_root` (keccak256 02), which is `path_fold` without one. `layer_root` stays, for
the callers that watch. `verify`'s `and_then(..).is_some_and(..)` becomes two `let .. else`s: no
codeword on either layer is `false`, otherwise the top root is compared with the key's. Not a
mechanical rewrite: the claim is that a fold whose visitor does nothing computes what the fold with
no visitor does. Tool bug: https://github.com/AeneasVerif/aeneas/issues/960.

`chain_ends` is the portable form in every build. The source has two: without `std`, a `from_fn` of
`chain` per chain; with `std`, every chain a step at a time, each step one batch through
`th_digests_many`. The extraction, and the proof of `verify`, cover the first only. The second
stays, for tests only, as `chain_ends_batched`. They agree on digits below `CHAIN_LEN`, which is
all `codeword` gives; on a larger digit the portable form's `CHAIN_LEN - 1 - start` underflows and
the batched one returns the value as it is, a difference `wots_leaf` cannot reach.

Tests: three, all under `std`.
layer_root_unwatched_matches_layer_root, against `layer_root` with a counting visitor, on both
layers of two real signatures whose leaf indices between them take both children at every level:
the same codeword and root, one call a level; with a path node changed, the same other root; with
a message whose digest is no codeword, `None` from both and no call.
chain_ends_matches_the_batched_one, the evidence that the form a `std` build runs agrees with the
one proved: on both layers and three keys, nine words that put every digit value on every chain,
and a signature's own codeword (checked to sum to `T` and hold every digit value) with its chain
values, where both also equal the key's chain ends computed by `chain`.
verify_matches_the_source, against `verify` copied from the source, on a real signature: accepted;
refused with no codeword at the bottom, with none at the top, and with another root at the top.
mutation: `layer_root_unwatched`'s node level `+ 1` -> layer_root_unwatched_matches_layer_root
fails; its path index `^ 1` -> it fails; `chain_ends` walking every chain from position 0 ->
chain_ends_matches_the_batched_one fails; `chain_ends` one step short -> it fails; `verify`
accepting where the bottom has no codeword (`return true`) -> verify_matches_the_source fails; the
same at the top -> it fails; `verify`'s top layer checked against the message, not the bottom
root -> it fails.

